# Netlify Redirects
#
# No catch-all rules here on purpose.
# Netlify automatically serves /404.html for unknown paths, so a rule like
# `/*    /404.html   404` is not needed. It is actively harmful on a
# multi-page static site: it intercepts Netlify's internal pretty-URL
# resolution (/about -> about.html) and returns "Page not found" for every
# page except the home page.
#
# Add only explicit rules below this line, e.g.:
# /old-page    /about.html    301
